{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The proposed front porch, by reason of its design, scale and siting, is considered to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;present an incongruous appearance that would unduly dominate the property&#x27;s&amp;nbsp;facade and, consequently, disrupt the prevailing pattern within the streetscene which is detrimental to the character and appearance of the surrounding area&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;As such, the proposed development is contrary to:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;-National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; -Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; -Policies SP2 and DMD1 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Whilst&amp;nbsp;the proposal would&amp;nbsp;contribute to the housing stock in the borough by 1, this is considered to have a minimal impact considering it is not a family-sized dwelling which the borough demands due to an identified shortfall. This is in contrast to the approved previously approved family sized dwelling at the site which would contribute more positively to the borough&#x27;s housing stock and addressing the shortfall. Instead, it would significantly reduce the internal and external amenity space of the existing 3 bedroom family-sized dwelling house at the site.&amp;nbsp; As such, the proposal is considered to be at the detriment of the existing family dwelling and/or the approved family dwelling at the site and is contrary to the following policies:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Policies D6 and H9 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Policies DMH5 and SP3 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
